# Obsidian vault I/O (local Windows)

**Brain:** `D:\Obsidian\Obsidian\00_Brain`  
**Project vaults:** `D:\Obsidian\Obsidian\40_VSCode\<Project>\`

## Mandatory tool choice (desk / local Cursor)

| Action | Tool | Do not use |
|--------|------|------------|
| Read / search vault | Native `Read` / `Grep` on `D:\Obsidian\...` | Any vault MCP (`petralian-obsidian`, `obsidian-brain`, filesystem MCP on `D:\`) |
| Write / edit vault | Native `Write` / `StrReplace` on `D:\Obsidian\...` | Any vault MCP |
| Repo code | Native workspace tools | — |

**Local policy:** MCP servers in `.cursor/mcp.json` are **not** for vault file I/O. Do not register `petralian-obsidian`, `obsidian-brain`, or filesystem MCP pointed at `D:\Obsidian\...` on the desk machine.

## Remote (cloud / iPhone)

| Action | Tool |
|--------|------|
| Read vault ops subset | Native `Read` / `Grep` on `vault-petralian` clone (`repositoryDependencies`) |
| Write vault ops subset | Commit/push in clone or hand off to desk Obsidian Git |
| Optional MCP on clone | Filesystem MCP on `${workspaceFolder}/../vault-petralian` — **Dashboard / cloud only**, never on `D:\` |

URL-based MCP (e.g. OpenSEO) is fine on cloud/mobile. Stdio MCP (Context7, Serena) is **desktop-only**.

## Other MCP

Context7, Serena, OpenSEO, etc. per `docs/TOKEN-STACK.md` — **never** for vault file I/O at desk.

**One tool per vault file per turn.** Never Read a file via MCP if you already read it natively this turn.
